  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) only reaches 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. With only two data points, the largest uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation can substantially improve over the PCA baseline. Question: config_007 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001—only the RNA encoder changes. scgpt is a pretrained generative model for single-cell data that may capture richer biological structure than linear PCA. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It isolates the effect of representation quality on the dominant modality without confounding with profile, aggregation, or fusion changes. (2) The outcome directly guides all subsequent experiments—if scgpt substantially improves, we exploit that encoder across profile/fusion settings; if it does not, PCA is competitive and we pivot to testing multiprofile/aggregation or multimodal fusion. (3) Under a limited budget, resolving whether learned representations matter for the primary signal source is the highest-information single experiment available."
}

